  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Consider an ideal gas confined in an isolated closed chamber. As the gas undergoes an adiabatic expansion, the average time of collision between molecules increases as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></msup></math> , where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math> is the volume of the gas. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math> is:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">P</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "CH04u",
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&gamma;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "UtLUA",
      "text": "<math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>3</mn> <mi>&gamma;</mi> <mo>+</mo> <mn>5</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>6</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "cSp1j",
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&gamma;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "KoECc",
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For an adiabatic process <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo></math> constant.<br />We know that average time of collision between molecules</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#964;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>&#960;</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>rms</mi></msub><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>where, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;number of molecules per unit volume <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>rms</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo></math> rms velocity of molecules</p><p>As <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8733;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>V</mi></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>rms</mi></msub><mo>&#8733;</mo><msqrt><mi>T</mi></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#964;</mi><mo>&#8733;</mo><mfrac><mi>V</mi><msqrt><mi>T</mi></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p>Thus, we can write</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>rms</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mi>T</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math>.</p><p>where, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> are constants.</p><p>For adiabatic process, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo></math> constant. Thus, we can write</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#964;</mi><mo>&#8733;</mo><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo>&#8733;</mo><mi>V</mi><msup><mfenced><msup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#947;</mi></mrow></msup></mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math></p><p>or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#964;</mi><mo>&#8733;</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math></p>",
